---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const receipt=core.orders.find(o=>o.order_id===103)!;
const lines=core.order_items.filter(l=>l.order_id===receipt.order_id);
const products=lines.map(l=>core.products.find(p=>p.product_id===l.product_id)!);
const customer=core.customers.find(c=>c.customer_id===receipt.customer_id)!;
---
<figure class="routing" aria-labelledby="r26-routing-title">
 <figcaption id="r26-routing-title"><span>Figure 1</span> The shop key decides where the request goes</figcaption>
 <shop-route>
  <div class="choices" role="group" aria-label="Request to route"><button data-query="receipt" aria-pressed="true">Shop 10’s order 103</button><button data-query="mug" aria-pressed="false">P7 without a shop</button><button data-query="catalogue" aria-pressed="false">Both shops’ products</button></div>
  <p class="request" data-request>Request carries shop_id = 10 → shard A</p>
  <div class="shards">
   <section data-shard="a" class="selected"><p class="panel-title">Shard A · shop 10</p><p class="route-label" data-route-a>↓ read here</p>
    <table><caption>products · every row has shop_id 10</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">product_id</th><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Price</th></tr></thead><tbody>{products.map(p=><tr><th scope="row">{p.product_id}</th><td>{p.name}</td><td>{p.price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    <table><caption>orders · shop_id 10</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">order_id</th><th scope="col">customer_id</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">{receipt.order_id}</th><td>{receipt.customer_id}</td><td>{receipt.status}</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <table><caption>order_items · both lines have shop_id 10 and order_id 103</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">line_no</th><th scope="col">product_id</th><th scope="col">Quantity</th><th scope="col">unit_price</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lines.map(l=><tr><th scope="row">{l.line_no}</th><td>{l.product_id}</td><td>{l.quantity}</td><td>{l.unit_price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    <p class="references">The order’s customer_id {receipt.customer_id} identifies {customer.name} in customers. Both lines refer to the order above through shop_id 10 and order_id 103. Their product references use that same shop_id: P7 reaches Blue mug; P3 reaches Green tea, 50 g.</p>
   </section>
   <section data-shard="b"><p class="panel-title">Shard B · shop 20</p><p class="route-label" data-route-b>Not contacted</p>
    <table><caption>products · shop_id 20</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">product_id</th><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">P7</th><td>Copper mug</td><td>18.00</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <p class="references">This P7 has shop_id 20. It cannot satisfy a line’s product reference carrying shop_id 10.</p><p class="scope">Other shop 20 rows are outside this drawing.</p>
   </section>
  </div>
  <p class="result" data-result aria-live="polite">The receipt’s order, lines and products are all on shard A. Shop 20’s P7 cannot join to shop 10’s line.</p>
 </shop-route>
 <p class="caption">A chosen tenant-placement model, with selected rows from the tenant-scoped schema. Every related table is deliberately placed by shop_id, and a router knows each shop’s owner. Real engines need corresponding distribution and co-location configuration; primary-key syntax alone does not produce these boxes. Replicas and individual storage ranges are omitted.</p>
 <details><summary>Routing in words</summary><p>A request scoped to shop 10 reaches A. P7 without a shop could mean either mug, so this scheme must ask A and B. A list across both shops also asks both and combines their results. On A, both order lines refer to order 103 in shop 10. Their product references reach shop 10’s P7 and P3. Shop 20’s P7 has a different shop_id, so it cannot match those references.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 class ShopRoute extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback(){
   if(this.dataset.ready)return;this.dataset.ready='true';
   const cases={receipt:['Request carries shop_id = 10 → shard A','The receipt’s order, lines and products are all on shard A. Shop 20’s P7 cannot join to shop 10’s line.'],mug:['Request carries product_id = P7, with no shop → shards A and B','Two different products match: (10, P7), Blue mug at 20.00; (20, P7), Copper mug at 18.00. P7 alone is not a global identity.'],catalogue:['Request spans shop_id IN (10, 20) → shards A and B','Both shards contribute rows. The coordinator combines the results; a required global order or limit must apply to that combined answer.']};
   for(const button of this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-query]'))button.addEventListener('click',()=>{
    const key=button.dataset.query as keyof typeof cases;const both=key!=='receipt';
    for(const b of this.querySelectorAll('button'))b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b===button));
    this.querySelector('[data-request]')!.textContent=cases[key][0];this.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=cases[key][1];
    this.querySelector('[data-shard=b]')!.classList.toggle('selected',both);this.querySelector('[data-route-b]')!.textContent=both?'↓ read here':'Not contacted';
   });
  }
 }
 if(!customElements.get('shop-route'))customElements.define('shop-route',ShopRoute);
</script>
<style>
.routing{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.6rem}shop-route{display:block;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:1rem}.choices{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem}.choices button{font:.85rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}.choices button[aria-pressed=true]{border:2px solid var(--color-accent);font-weight:700}.choices button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.request{font:.95rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);padding:.8rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.shards{display:grid;gap:1rem}.shards section{margin:0;border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.shards section.selected{border:2px solid var(--color-accent)}.panel-title{font:600 .95rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);margin:0}.route-label{font:.8rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);min-height:1.5rem}.shards table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin:1rem 0;font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}.shards caption{text-align:left;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.shards th,.shards td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.45rem .3rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.shards thead th{font-weight:500}.references,.scope{font:.82rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}.scope{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.result{font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .8rem;min-height:4.5rem}.caption,details{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){.shards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.choices button{width:100%}.result{min-height:0}}
</style>
